xcb: drop the cached clipboard formats when another client takes the selection

Harmattan's clipboard manager (/usr/bin/clipboard) takes CLIPBOARD over right after every copy,
with the copy's own timestamp. Qt reset its cached formats only for a strictly newer timestamp,
so after a clear() (the edit bubble clears after a paste, as in Qt 4) the formats cached while the
clipboard was empty stayed, and the next paste got nothing.

diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/xcb/qxcbclipboard.cpp b/src/plugins/platforms/xcb/qxcbclipboard.cpp
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/xcb/qxcbclipboard.cpp	2026-09-26 17:47:57.826042425 +0200
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/xcb/qxcbclipboard.cpp	2026-09-26 17:47:57.827397868 +0200
@@ -672,7 +672,11 @@
     // Note1: Here we care only about the xfixes events that come from other processes.
     // Note2: If the QClipboard::clear() is issued, event->owner is XCB_NONE,
     // so we check selection_timestamp to not handle our own QClipboard::clear().
-    if (event->owner != owner() && event->selection_timestamp > m_timestamp[mode]) {
+    // Harmattan: another owner always means new data. The clipboard manager takes the
+    // selection over right after a copy with the copy's own timestamp, and with the check
+    // the formats cached while it was empty stayed: paste got nothing after a clear().
+    if (event->owner != owner()
+            && (event->owner != XCB_NONE || event->selection_timestamp > m_timestamp[mode])) {
         if (!m_xClipboard[mode]) {
             m_xClipboard[mode].reset(new QXcbClipboardMime(mode, this));
         } else {
